1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,840
I still remember it clearly.

2
00:00:06,840 --> 00:00:09,380
It was like something from another world.

3
00:00:11,260 --> 00:00:15,500
The Golden City, where things that are beyond human live.

4
00:00:17,020 --> 00:00:21,920
The place was boundless and vast and overwhelming.

5
00:00:22,780 --> 00:00:25,080
It was beyond anything we could handle.

6
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:27,040
Sure is hot.

7
00:00:27,040 --> 00:00:32,380
So that rumor about a city of gold at the bottom of the netherworld.

8
00:00:32,720 --> 00:00:33,060
Yeah.

9
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:36,360
I bet someone saw this and saw it a mail balloon.

10
00:00:44,440 --> 00:00:46,680
What is this?

11
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:48,180
A building?

12
00:00:50,460 --> 00:00:52,200
Try to be careful, okay?

13
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:53,020
Sorry.

14
00:00:53,860 --> 00:00:55,960
Look at this, it's some kind of crystal.

15
00:00:55,960 --> 00:00:57,380
Did you hurt yourself?

16
00:00:57,760 --> 00:00:58,420
I'm fine.

17
00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:03,680
And check this out.

18
00:01:03,840 --> 00:01:05,340
It's like it's mixed into the building.

19
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:07,540
Oh, wow.

20
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:08,440
Incredible.

21
00:01:08,940 --> 00:01:10,700
How do you think this place was made?

22
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:14,380
Did the surface collapse and get swallowed up a long time ago?

23
00:01:14,760 --> 00:01:17,140
Did the whole city get turned into a fossil?

24
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:20,140
Or is it a mirage created by the crystals?

25
00:01:21,140 --> 00:01:22,620
Guess there's no way to be sure.

26
00:01:22,620 --> 00:01:24,800
But it's beautiful.

27
00:01:24,980 --> 00:01:26,880
But it's beautiful.

28
00:01:27,040 --> 00:01:27,300
Yeah.

29
00:02:57,052 --> 00:03:27,032
To be continued...

30
00:03:27,052 --> 00:03:30,472
Must mean we're supposed to blaze our own trail, huh?

31
00:03:31,412 --> 00:03:35,532
In that case, I'll walk in front since I'm able to see the movements of the force field.

32
00:03:36,112 --> 00:03:37,872
You just give us the orders, team leader.

33
00:03:39,132 --> 00:03:39,892
Team leader?

34
00:03:40,652 --> 00:03:44,352
How are your injuries holding up, Greg? Are you able to take the rear?

35
00:03:44,772 --> 00:03:46,532
No problem. Leave it to me.

36
00:03:47,672 --> 00:03:51,952
Come to think of it, all four of us managed to make it down here just fine, didn't we?

37
00:03:52,952 --> 00:03:53,312
Mia!

38
00:03:53,312 --> 00:03:58,092
That would mean White Whistles don't necessarily have to come on their own.

39
00:03:58,292 --> 00:04:02,392
Now that you mention it, that bunch does like to make up their own rules, don't they?

40
00:04:02,792 --> 00:04:05,332
We can just ask the next White Whistle we come across.

41
00:04:05,552 --> 00:04:09,052
You can't be serious. I bet they'd just be another scoundrel.

42
00:04:09,052 --> 00:04:17,032
The sixth layer. The world of the absolute boundary from which no human can return.

43
00:04:17,032 --> 00:04:26,272
A turbinate dragon.

44
00:04:26,752 --> 00:04:29,992
They have terrible poisonous scales that rupture when struck.

45
00:04:30,372 --> 00:04:34,252
And it says that the males fight by aggressively slamming into each other.

46
00:04:34,812 --> 00:04:38,952
They're very tenacious and move freely in three dimensions without any regard to the curse.

47
00:04:39,512 --> 00:04:40,212
Pretty scary.

48
00:04:40,212 --> 00:04:45,692
It says in the sixth layer, one of them is as dangerous as a swarm of amaranthine deceptors.

49
00:04:45,972 --> 00:04:47,492
Nah, pass on that.

50
00:04:49,112 --> 00:04:51,932
Oh, these guys. Must be Mizojacks.

51
00:04:52,912 --> 00:04:56,172
It says they live near geothermals and are calm.

52
00:04:56,812 --> 00:04:59,132
Geothermals? I don't see anything like that here.

53
00:04:59,392 --> 00:05:00,572
Does it say how they taste?

54
00:05:01,092 --> 00:05:03,252
It says their freshly laid eggs are pretty good.

55
00:05:03,252 --> 00:05:13,612
Hey, come here, guys!

56
00:05:13,992 --> 00:05:14,992
I found some eggs!

57
00:05:16,652 --> 00:05:17,992
Oh, they're moving!

58
00:05:18,592 --> 00:05:20,952
Those don't seem like they're very freshly laid.

59
00:05:21,192 --> 00:05:24,432
Well, maybe my mother never ate any just before they started hatching.

60
00:05:24,952 --> 00:05:27,072
You want to try to eat some?

61
00:05:27,072 --> 00:05:38,592
You see that? What is that light?

62
00:05:38,592 --> 00:06:01,632
What's that?

63
00:06:06,492 --> 00:06:08,352
Poison gas! Don't breathe it in!

64
00:06:08,352 --> 00:06:15,392
What is that?

65
00:06:15,732 --> 00:06:17,652
Time to run! Right now, guys!

66
00:06:26,052 --> 00:06:26,652
Hurry!

67
00:06:30,072 --> 00:06:32,932
Were those the geothermals she mentioned?

68
00:06:33,712 --> 00:06:36,092
What a terrible place to make a nest.

69
00:06:36,092 --> 00:06:38,712
They were like huge bubbles, weren't they?

70
00:06:39,092 --> 00:06:41,932
Oh, Riko, why does it sound like you're actually enjoying this?

71
00:06:43,972 --> 00:06:44,632
Ta-da!

72
00:06:45,872 --> 00:06:46,432
Whoa!

73
00:06:46,852 --> 00:06:48,592
They made it through that without breaking?

74
00:06:48,872 --> 00:06:49,812
Sure are strong!

75
00:06:49,812 --> 00:06:55,352
How is it?

76
00:06:55,352 --> 00:06:57,392
Should be fine if we boil it.

77
00:07:03,032 --> 00:07:04,592
I'm so hungry.

78
00:07:05,232 --> 00:07:06,472
Hurry up and open it.

79
00:07:06,472 --> 00:07:20,992
It's still alive even after we boiled it?

80
00:07:21,212 --> 00:07:22,112
I don't know.

81
00:07:22,212 --> 00:07:23,112
Looks dead to me.

82
00:07:23,692 --> 00:07:25,272
Maybe it's just a reflex.

83
00:07:25,972 --> 00:07:28,432
Boiling must not be enough to break down their muscles.

84
00:07:28,432 --> 00:07:31,212
I wonder what sort of body they have.

85
00:07:31,612 --> 00:07:33,732
I would have preferred a freshly laid one.

86
00:07:33,732 --> 00:07:39,772
Are you for real?

87
00:07:39,772 --> 00:07:41,612
You're actually going to try it?

88
00:07:45,612 --> 00:07:47,912
It's moving inside my mouth.

89
00:07:48,172 --> 00:07:48,992
Is it any good?

90
00:07:48,992 --> 00:07:54,852
Can you give it a little flavor?

91
00:07:56,132 --> 00:07:59,532
If you do a good job, Nanachi might do it again.

92
00:07:59,792 --> 00:08:00,652
What the heck?

93
00:08:00,772 --> 00:08:01,852
What do you mean by that?

94
00:08:03,252 --> 00:08:04,332
Riko, no!

95
00:08:04,572 --> 00:08:05,932
I don't want that thing!

96
00:08:06,712 --> 00:08:07,972
Smash this up.

97
00:08:09,152 --> 00:08:09,912
Coat everything.

98
00:08:10,612 --> 00:08:11,692
And then cook it.

99
00:08:11,692 --> 00:08:17,432
It's still moving.

100
00:08:18,352 --> 00:08:20,772
But I admit it does smell really good.

101
00:08:25,232 --> 00:08:25,832
Great.

102
00:08:26,032 --> 00:08:27,552
Pretty good once you get used to it.

103
00:08:38,732 --> 00:08:39,972
Was it too hot?

104
00:08:39,972 --> 00:08:41,732
Uh, so hot.

105
00:08:43,832 --> 00:08:44,272
Huh?

106
00:08:47,872 --> 00:08:48,912
We did it!

107
00:08:53,212 --> 00:08:54,992
Here, just try to slow down a little.

108
00:08:57,292 --> 00:09:00,792
I gotta say, it feels like I've eaten this stuff somewhere else before, you know?

109
00:09:01,172 --> 00:09:02,852
Well, I have no memory of it.

110
00:09:05,752 --> 00:09:07,132
Oh, I remember now!

111
00:09:07,612 --> 00:09:08,692
At the orphanage!

112
00:09:08,692 --> 00:09:10,292
On Cave Reading Memorial Day!

113
00:09:10,372 --> 00:09:11,052
A foreign...

114
00:09:11,052 --> 00:09:12,212
What was it again?

115
00:09:12,592 --> 00:09:13,372
I forget.

116
00:09:14,112 --> 00:09:15,752
But this tastes like the thing we cooked!

117
00:09:16,532 --> 00:09:17,292
And Nat!

118
00:09:17,632 --> 00:09:20,352
He liked it so much he even tried to take other people's.

119
00:09:20,892 --> 00:09:21,712
Who's Nat?

120
00:09:21,972 --> 00:09:23,212
We mentioned him before.

121
00:09:23,432 --> 00:09:24,872
He's one of our friends from Worth.

122
00:09:24,872 --> 00:09:25,592
Ah!

123
00:09:28,092 --> 00:09:28,572
Nat!

124
00:09:31,152 --> 00:09:31,592
Shiki!

125
00:09:32,132 --> 00:09:32,532
Kiwi!

126
00:09:33,992 --> 00:09:34,652
And Jiduo!

127
00:09:35,252 --> 00:09:37,292
I wonder if everyone's doing all right.

128
00:09:37,932 --> 00:09:41,692
Even if you worry about him, it's not like you'll ever get to see him again, you know?

129
00:09:44,212 --> 00:09:48,332
Still, as long as you're in the Abyss, you Cave Raiders are forever connected.

130
00:09:48,332 --> 00:09:53,652
Rico, if it's weighing on you, why don't you send them a letter again?

131
00:09:55,292 --> 00:09:55,992
That's right!

132
00:09:56,412 --> 00:09:57,332
Let's send them a letter!

133
00:09:58,292 --> 00:10:01,112
This is the sixth layer of the Abyss, after all!

134
00:10:01,252 --> 00:10:03,792
We have to let them know about Team Rico's achievements!

135
00:10:03,792 --> 00:10:11,652
Sure, but can't we do something about the name Team Rico?

136
00:10:12,132 --> 00:10:13,172
It's boring.

137
00:10:13,692 --> 00:10:15,512
Well, we'll use it till we think of something better.

138
00:10:15,832 --> 00:10:17,772
Sometimes you're way too laid back, Rico.

139
00:10:18,152 --> 00:10:21,072
Like whenever we first met, she named me for a dog.

140
00:10:21,272 --> 00:10:23,012
Well, you are kind of like a dog, right?

141
00:10:23,892 --> 00:10:24,372
Here.

142
00:10:24,872 --> 00:10:25,552
All done.

143
00:10:26,252 --> 00:10:26,772
Wow!

144
00:10:27,612 --> 00:10:29,192
Thank you so much, Nanachi!

145
00:10:29,752 --> 00:10:30,372
You sure?

146
00:10:30,592 --> 00:10:32,012
Should you be in the sketch?

147
00:10:32,332 --> 00:10:33,252
Come on!

148
00:10:33,252 --> 00:10:36,452
Like anyone could actually come down here and pursue us.

149
00:10:37,132 --> 00:10:37,572
All right.

150
00:10:37,872 --> 00:10:40,672
The Higa oil to keep bugs and birds away is good to go!

151
00:10:41,292 --> 00:10:43,412
I hope they can handle this bail load.

152
00:10:43,872 --> 00:10:44,212
Mm-hmm.

153
00:10:45,292 --> 00:10:46,212
Shigi once said,

154
00:10:46,692 --> 00:10:50,512
the odds of a mail balloon reaching them from the deeper depths are extremely low.

155
00:10:51,852 --> 00:10:54,592
I wonder if that last mail balloon ever got there.

156
00:10:55,512 --> 00:10:58,572
And that said, is it even possible to make it from this far?

157
00:10:59,312 --> 00:11:00,672
You know, here in the Abyss,

158
00:11:00,672 --> 00:11:04,212
one's mindset has the ability to openly manifest itself.

159
00:11:04,552 --> 00:11:05,172
Now, Reg!

160
00:11:08,792 --> 00:11:11,972
If your fears can take shape and manifest in your body,

161
00:11:12,432 --> 00:11:15,372
then couldn't your wishes also take shape and become reality?

162
00:11:15,372 --> 00:11:19,072
Let's just believe that the first one made it,

163
00:11:19,252 --> 00:11:21,292
and this one is going to reach them as well.

164
00:11:22,692 --> 00:11:23,172
Yeah.

165
00:11:23,172 --> 00:11:39,332
The bird repellent didn't work on those guys, did it?

166
00:11:39,332 --> 00:11:41,632
Don't worry about it.

167
00:11:41,632 --> 00:11:45,232
I bet your mom screwed up plenty of times like that before, too.

168
00:11:45,952 --> 00:11:47,632
Let's hit the sack for the night.

169
00:11:47,752 --> 00:11:48,092
Yeah.

170
00:11:48,452 --> 00:11:49,952
I'll just soak in bed.

171
00:11:49,952 --> 00:12:19,932
The bird repellent didn't work on those guys.

172
00:12:19,952 --> 00:12:44,332
What's going on here?

173
00:12:44,332 --> 00:12:47,412
She's gone!

174
00:12:48,212 --> 00:12:49,672
She's not here!

175
00:12:50,752 --> 00:12:51,832
Krushka's not here!

176
00:12:52,032 --> 00:12:53,372
Even though I was wearing her!

177
00:12:54,212 --> 00:12:55,452
Where is she?

178
00:13:00,072 --> 00:13:02,652
Someone snatched the mail balloon from that bird.

179
00:13:03,332 --> 00:13:05,672
Tracked us without me sensing their consciousness.

180
00:13:06,832 --> 00:13:09,012
Got through Reg's arm trap with ease.

181
00:13:09,772 --> 00:13:11,512
And made a mess of things.

182
00:13:13,712 --> 00:13:17,772
I don't know who we're dealing with or even what it is they want from us.

183
00:13:22,012 --> 00:13:22,532
Iron.

184
00:13:23,332 --> 00:13:25,092
But it isn't blood that's on here.

185
00:13:25,832 --> 00:13:27,532
It's got some kind of mineral.

186
00:13:27,532 --> 00:13:31,032
And I smell some fat mixed in there, too.

187
00:13:35,612 --> 00:13:38,372
Going to the extra trouble of leaving clues behind.

188
00:13:38,752 --> 00:13:40,092
They're taking us for idiots.

189
00:13:41,552 --> 00:13:42,832
Let's get going, then.

190
00:13:43,112 --> 00:13:44,672
We're going to get Prushka back.

191
00:13:44,672 --> 00:13:51,292
No changes in the force field.

192
00:13:51,972 --> 00:13:53,432
Prushka's scent is still there.

193
00:13:53,772 --> 00:13:55,012
Faint, but still present.

194
00:14:10,372 --> 00:14:11,172
This way.

195
00:14:11,172 --> 00:14:12,932
Good doggy.

196
00:14:21,932 --> 00:14:27,212
Hey, guys.

197
00:14:27,672 --> 00:14:29,532
Mania just found something.

198
00:14:30,172 --> 00:14:30,652
Whoa.

199
00:14:31,012 --> 00:14:31,972
Look at this.

200
00:14:32,292 --> 00:14:34,572
Must be the remains of some small animals.

201
00:14:35,092 --> 00:14:38,872
Does this little thing have its butt sewn shut?

202
00:14:38,872 --> 00:14:58,892
Mixed in with the flesh and fat.

203
00:14:59,272 --> 00:15:00,652
There's something else in here.

204
00:15:02,572 --> 00:15:03,632
Is that...

205
00:15:03,632 --> 00:15:05,132
It looks like hair, right?

206
00:15:05,132 --> 00:15:08,512
Can you follow their trail using that?

207
00:15:08,872 --> 00:15:11,712
What's wrong?

208
00:15:12,052 --> 00:15:12,632
What is it?

209
00:15:12,992 --> 00:15:13,532
Oh, no.

210
00:15:13,892 --> 00:15:14,552
No way.

211
00:15:15,612 --> 00:15:18,052
This came from you and Riko, Nanachi.

212
00:15:18,052 --> 00:15:23,552
Oh, my God.

213
00:15:23,772 --> 00:15:24,492
He's right.

214
00:15:25,432 --> 00:15:26,572
Riko's pigtail.

215
00:15:27,532 --> 00:15:28,812
And my tail hairs.

216
00:15:29,652 --> 00:15:32,492
They plucked other spots, too, trying not to be noticeable.

217
00:15:33,032 --> 00:15:36,192
They did whatever they wanted, assaulting us as we slept there unaware.

218
00:15:36,692 --> 00:15:37,172
Damn them.

219
00:15:37,992 --> 00:15:38,432
Irredeemable.

220
00:15:38,432 --> 00:15:42,972
Hey, maybe we should stop and take a moment to regroup.

221
00:15:45,472 --> 00:15:46,472
Let's get going.

222
00:15:46,732 --> 00:15:48,612
We can't let something like this scare us.

223
00:15:49,432 --> 00:15:50,212
Nya!

224
00:15:58,672 --> 00:15:59,072
Baby!

225
00:16:01,172 --> 00:16:05,972
Oh, my God.

226
00:16:06,252 --> 00:16:07,632
Can't believe me?

227
00:16:08,552 --> 00:16:09,232
Oh, my God.

228
00:16:09,492 --> 00:16:11,432
He was wrong.

229
00:16:11,432 --> 00:16:12,352
His soul's DNA surprised.

230
00:16:12,352 --> 00:16:13,952
He was amber and he was more damaged.

231
00:16:13,952 --> 00:16:15,192
I was not sorry for his wain.

232
00:16:15,192 --> 00:16:17,892
I think his soul was bigger and前.

233
00:16:17,892 --> 00:16:27,012
Footprints

234
00:16:27,012 --> 00:16:29,532
Bipedal

235
00:16:29,532 --> 00:16:31,152
And seems really big

236
00:16:31,152 --> 00:16:33,432
So, is this who we're after?

237
00:16:33,892 --> 00:16:34,692
I can't tell

238
00:16:34,692 --> 00:16:37,392
But we all seem to be headed in the same direction

239
00:16:37,392 --> 00:16:39,392
They're moving upwind

240
00:16:39,392 --> 00:16:40,872
Toward where the scent is stronger

241
00:16:40,872 --> 00:16:42,232
Let's go

242
00:16:47,892 --> 00:17:12,372
This must be it

243
00:17:12,372 --> 00:17:16,532
Well, I've got a hunch we're about to have an encounter

244
00:17:16,532 --> 00:17:18,832
Another structure

245
00:17:18,832 --> 00:17:20,652
Some sort of tower

246
00:17:20,652 --> 00:17:24,152
It almost looks like the carcass of some creature

247
00:17:24,152 --> 00:17:27,152
Hey, you guys

248
00:17:27,152 --> 00:17:29,712
Do you notice anything?

249
00:17:30,992 --> 00:17:33,152
To the top right of the entrance

250
00:17:33,152 --> 00:17:37,852
It's that symbol

251
00:17:37,852 --> 00:17:39,632
The one marked on our picture

252
00:17:39,632 --> 00:17:43,052
What's it mean, Nanaji?

253
00:17:43,652 --> 00:17:45,332
Beats the heck out of me, but

254
00:17:45,332 --> 00:17:46,692
Let's go

255
00:17:46,692 --> 00:17:48,992
We are gonna get our Prushka back

256
00:17:48,992 --> 00:17:50,532
Yeah, Riko, you said it

257
00:17:50,532 --> 00:17:53,712
Luckily, the ground leading to that entrance is pretty level

258
00:17:53,712 --> 00:17:56,512
No need to worry about the streams coming or going

259
00:17:56,512 --> 00:17:58,672
Interesting

260
00:17:58,672 --> 00:18:05,032
All this stuff's new to me

261
00:18:05,032 --> 00:18:06,772
Are you two ready for this?

262
00:18:07,072 --> 00:18:07,632
Nah

263
00:18:07,632 --> 00:18:11,032
We'll at least make a lot of smoke as we make our way there

264
00:18:11,032 --> 00:18:12,852
Counting on you if things go bad

265
00:18:12,852 --> 00:18:14,252
I'll take care of it

266
00:18:14,252 --> 00:18:14,432
I'll take care of it

267
00:18:14,432 --> 00:18:21,112
Now, you two better get ready for this

268
00:18:21,112 --> 00:18:21,692
Uh-huh

269
00:18:21,692 --> 00:18:37,632
Did you hear that, Nanaji?

270
00:18:37,632 --> 00:18:39,272
Hear what?

271
00:18:39,692 --> 00:18:40,192
Tell me

272
00:18:40,192 --> 00:18:43,332
Nah, but I have no idea where it's coming from

273
00:18:43,332 --> 00:18:45,792
It does kind of sound like a person's voice, though

274
00:18:45,792 --> 00:18:46,932
